# Q3: Structure M1: `pose` (neutral) -> `pose` (interrupt, short duration) -> `path` (base lunge) -> `pose` (hold). This creates a clear sequence of arm-up, then body-forward, which is very readable and forceful, and fixes the static nature of the previous attempt.
# Q4: The transition to the interrupt pose must be fast (duration ~0.4s), and the subsequent base lunge must also be fast (speed ~4.0). A final hold of at least 1.5 seconds is needed to maintain the "stop" signal.
